# claudeide.nvim Development Rules

## Architecture
This is a pure-Lua WebSocket server implementing the Model Context Protocol (MCP).
It makes Neovim act as an IDE server so Claude CLI can connect via `/ide`.

## Key Subsystems
- `lua/claudeide/server/` — TCP, HTTP upgrade, WebSocket frames (vim.uv based)
- `lua/claudeide/mcp.lua` — JSON-RPC 2.0 message routing
- `lua/claudeide/tools.lua` — MCP tool implementations (openFile, openDiff)
- `lua/claudeide/diff.lua` — Blocking diff UI with accept/deny
- `lua/claudeide/lockfile.lua` — Lock file management at ~/.claude/ide/
- `lua/claudeide/selection.lua` — Selection change notification broadcasting

## Constraints
- No external dependencies — all networking is via vim.uv (libuv bindings)
- Protocol version: 2025-03-26
- JSON-RPC 2.0 over WebSocket (binary frames, not text)
- Lock file ideName: "TikTok VimPlugin"
- Must handle multiple simultaneous client connections
- All blocking operations (like diff accept/deny) use coroutines or callbacks, never synchronous waits
